00:01:55.720 --> 00:02:00.360
The first time I saw Hanami, I immediately
thought that this is one of the most badass

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:04.990
character designs I have seen in a while...because
I mean!

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:10.810
The muscular white body the hidden arm, the
helmet like head with the teeth exposed and

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:16.410
finally the branches for eyes, I was absolutely
blown away by the design here.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:21.300
And on top of that it was speaking in this
eerie tongue, with a female voice by the way,

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:24.730
that gave it that vibe of something ancient
and mystical.

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:28.500
Even without knowing anything about this curse,
it radiated danger.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:32.780
By the way, did you know that if you reverse
what Hanami is saying you actually understand

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:37.540
what she's saying?

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:41.860
- Wut!?

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:47.510
Now the next time Hanami shoed up, I was completely
startled to see her approaching Gojo, the

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:53.130
strongest being alive, without being noticed,
use the by far most beautiful cursed technique

00:02:53.130 --> 00:03:03.650
in the story that drains away ones will 
to fight, - divert Gojo's attention by attacking

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:08.150
Itadori and actually being able to escape
with Jogo, who otherwise would have fallen

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:09.970
into the sorcerers hands.

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:14.550
I love the writing of this scene, because
we get so much power-scaling and set-up.

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:21.470
As soon as Jogo is introduced, despite his
power, he loses against Gojo, who fully demonstrates

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:24.760
his power.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:33.090
However, that same loss is used as an opportunity
to show how intelligent Hanami's way of thinking

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:34.370
and fighting is.

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:38.880
And even more than that, it shows us that
these curses actually care for one another.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:54.569
Hanami doesn't have to save Jogo, but she
does so anyway.

00:03:54.569 --> 00:03:59.130
- Keep this scene in mind, because it is really
important to what Hanami is all about.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:03.380
So at this point, Hanami was probably the
most intriguing curse for me that I wanted

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:04.380
to see more of.

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:10.319
As I explained in his video, Mahito's perfectly
written evil just creeps you out every time

00:04:10.319 --> 00:04:19.250
we see him, which made me really tense and
anxious every time we saw him fight.

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:24.690
His cruelty and childish attire make him a
wonderful horror element, but his scenes are

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:27.430
meant to upset and not please.

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:30.760
Hanami on the other hand I knew I wanted to
see in action.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:37.540
Her character promised an immensely enjoyable
and engaging fight, based on power and ability.

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:40.000
And oh boy did the story deliver.

