-

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:45.540
The battle during the exchange event, both
animation and plot wise, was some of the best

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.500
I have seen in anime to this point.

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:53.750
Finally, I saw Hanami fully express her personality
and powers, that did not disappoint.

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:59.570
Using a variety of nature based attacks, ranging
from cursed buds that suck out cursed energy,

00:05:59.570 --> 00:06:04.270
over floating wooden balls that allow her
to attack and levitate, to the manifestation

00:06:04.270 --> 00:06:09.479
fo enormous roots, that she can summon and
erase from reality, the special grade curse

00:06:09.479 --> 00:06:15.120
was able to take on six of the school's most
elite jujutsu students, rendering the majority

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:25.050
of them unable to fight after encountering
him.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:28.070
The plan I think, was pretty damn good.

00:06:28.070 --> 00:06:32.990
Use Hanami's unique abilities to hide her
presence to sneak into the arena and cause

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:38.990
chaos, distracting everyone enough to allow
Mahito to steal Sukuna'S fingers and the cursed

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:39.990
wombs.

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:45.320
Given her wide range attacks and sturdiness,
Hanami was the perfect candidate to buy time.

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:50.620
Once again, it took Gojo to make her retreat,
badly wounded from his attack, that I'm gonna

00:06:50.620 --> 00:07:06.270
show here, just because it's my favorite scene
of the first season.

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:12.820
- You can be sure that Gojo was pissed that
this curse manage to escape him twice already.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:17.790
What I found awesome here was that, while
the curses were successful in their mission,

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:24.180
this battle allowed many of the top students
to really shine, especially Todo and Itadori.

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:28.270
Itadori growing immensely in his use and control
of cursed energy.

00:07:28.270 --> 00:07:33.710
And Todo, as you hopefully remember from his
video, has an idealogical clash here with

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:34.710
Hanami.

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:39.520
Because Todo, while acknowledging the fleetingness
of things and the importance of being once

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:45.150
with nature, also believes in the ability
of humans to go against this and leave a lasting

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:53.370
impact on the world.

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:58.600
The reason Hanami is such a wonderful opponent
for Todo and his eternal love for his new

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:05.570
besto friendo Yuji, is that Hanami is the
embodiment of nature itself, which you think

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:10.150
might be trivial, but given the importance
of nature in the story, what I found is that

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:15.360
Akutami has actually given Hanami a very unique
position in the story in terms of Jujutsu

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:17.930
Kaisen's main take away message.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:26.759
- mahito explains where they com form -

00:08:26.759 --> 00:08:32.139
As Mahito explains here, Jogo, Hanami and
Dogon are curses born from humans fear of

00:08:32.139 --> 00:08:35.409
nature, the earth, the sea and the forest.

00:08:35.409 --> 00:08:39.959
And yet to me it seems like Hanami, takes
a bit of a special role within the curses,

00:08:39.959 --> 00:08:41.959
as the embodiment of living things.

00:08:41.959 --> 00:08:47.180
Mahito and Jogo want to destroy human dominance
in order to live out freely in the world as

00:08:47.180 --> 00:08:49.170
they please and rule.

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:54.009
They see themselves as the true humans and
as the superior race.

00:08:54.009 --> 00:08:57.749
Hanami shares that view, but has a different
desire.

00:08:57.749 --> 00:09:02.949
As a dark twist on Mother Nature,- that's
why I say her, see I promised it would make

00:09:02.949 --> 00:09:03.949
sense.

00:09:03.949 --> 00:09:07.879
As I was was saying, as Mother Nature, Hanami
seems to not only be born from humans fear

00:09:07.879 --> 00:09:15.839
of nature, but also of nature's wrath towards
humans.

00:09:15.839 --> 00:09:20.119
Based on all her dialogues, to me it seemed
pretty obvious that Akutami writes Hanami

00:09:20.119 --> 00:09:26.079
as a physical representation of nature fighting
back against all what we as a species have

00:09:26.079 --> 00:09:29.730
done to out planet, to all the living things
around us.

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:34.730
But isn't Hanami one of the bad guys?

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:42.690
Gojo actually describes Hanami's presence
as almost spirit like, and I think her life

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:50.389
based abilities support the idea, that she
is a mix between curse and spirit.

00:09:50.389 --> 00:09:57.720
Yes, she clearly has traits of a curse, her
wish to destroy humanity, her ability to suck

00:09:57.720 --> 00:10:02.959
life from the living things around her and
encouraged by Mahito, she even starts embracing

00:10:02.959 --> 00:10:12.149
her curse nature a bit more during the fight
with Todo and Yuji.

00:10:12.149 --> 00:10:18.579
And yet on the other side of things, I'm not
sure about you, but to me it never feels like

00:10:18.579 --> 00:10:22.379
Hanami was about to kill...pretty much anyone.

00:10:22.379 --> 00:10:28.199
The first words she speaks who Fushiguro,
Kamo and Inumaki is calling them children,

00:10:28.199 --> 00:10:29.469
as a mother would.

00:10:29.469 --> 00:10:34.589
- Hanami, who must be very ancient indeed,
until now clearly has wished to coexist with

00:10:34.589 --> 00:10:37.360
humanity and has come to a breaking point.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:40.370
Humanity is no longer bearable to nature.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:44.730
However her wish is to protect, not to hurt
humans.

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:49.949
Her name Hanami literally means cherry blossom
viewing in Japan, an activity associated with

00:10:49.949 --> 00:10:53.300
celebrating the beauty and fleetingness of
nature.

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:54.489
And wish getting shit-faced.

00:10:54.489 --> 00:10:55.869
But you get my point.

00:10:55.869 --> 00:11:00.490
Up to this fight, she purposefully has covered
up her left arm, that contrary to the pure

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:05.839
white of the rest of her body is dark black
and has a much more curse-like vibe, as it

00:11:05.839 --> 00:11:10.149
is the source of her ability to drain nature
itself.

00:11:10.149 --> 00:11:19.220
To me it looks like she clearly doesn't like
to associate herself with her curse powers.

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:24.959
Also right here, she clearly could have seriously
injured or even killed Fushiguro, but chose

00:11:24.959 --> 00:11:30.000
to only aim for the small little phone in
his hand to prevent the students form contacting

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.220
Gojo.

00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:41.779
Hanami's only weakness on her steelyard body,
are the two branches growing where eyes should

00:11:41.779 --> 00:11:42.779
be.

00:11:42.779 --> 00:11:47.619
These branches, symbolizing nature and its
softness, are her only weakness, once again

00:11:47.619 --> 00:11:56.439
showing the mix between spirit and curse.

00:11:56.439 --> 00:12:04.370
I mean Jogo doesn't have a weakness like this,
he has a volcano on his head.

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:05.370
-

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:08.790
And when I thought about it in the context
of the story, Hanami doesn't even properly

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:11.790
qualify as a villain.

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:16.470
Without saying that she is justified in her
actions, which I don't think she is, she still

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:26.370
has a more peaceful and noble approach to
life than many of the sorceres do.

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:30.029
And when you think about it don't you find
it interesting that the three most evil guys

00:12:30.029 --> 00:12:35.089
in the story so far, Sukuna, Mahito and Geto
are the most human ones?

00:12:35.089 --> 00:12:41.230
Hanami, Jogo and Cuthulu are pretty much exploited
for feeling emotions just as or maybe even

00:12:41.230 --> 00:12:44.889
stronger than humans.

00:12:44.889 --> 00:12:45.889
-

00:12:45.889 --> 00:12:50.139
That is the hidden meaning behind Hanami's
character.

00:12:50.139 --> 00:12:55.160
In the end even the curses only serve to highlight
how much we as humans can suck.

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:59.790
I believe that Akutami's message with Jujutsu
Kaisen is 1, finding out what it means to

00:12:59.790 --> 00:13:05.850
live a good live; 2, exploring the depth of
human morality and 3, he wants you to watch

00:13:05.850 --> 00:13:07.079
this video next.

